ents EpiAgent as a foundation model for single‑cell chromatin accessibility without mentioning natural‑language text, prompts, or documents, so no substantive text component or text‑bio bridge is evident. | The abstract introduces EpiAgent as a new foundation model pretrained on 5 M cells (large‑scale pretraining) but only describes encoding with a bidirectional attention mechanism, with no mention of decoder or generative capability.","The abstract presents EpiAgent as a foundation model for single‑cell chromatin accessibility without mentioning natural‑language text, prompts, or documents, so no substantive text component or text‑bio bridge is evident.","The abstract introduces EpiAgent as a new foundation model pretrained on 5 M cells (large‑scale pretraining) but only describes encoding with a bidirectional attention mechanism, with no mention of decoder or generative capability.",,EpiAgent: foundation model for single-cell epigenomics,"Abstract
