s a new foundation model for single‑cell chromatin accessibility (biological modality) but only tokenizes the data as “cell sentences” without natural‑language text, so there is no substantive text component or text‑bio bridge. | The abstract presents EpiAgent as a bidirectional encoder pretrained on a large scATAC corpus, with no mention of decoder or generative mechanisms, indicating no generative model; however it highlights extensive pretraining (5M cells, 35B tokens), satisfying foundation‑model evidence.","The work presents a new foundation model for single‑cell chromatin accessibility (biological modality) but only tokenizes the data as “cell sentences” without natural‑language text, so there is no substantive text component or text‑bio bridge.","The abstract presents EpiAgent as a bidirectional encoder pretrained on a large scATAC corpus, with no mention of decoder or generative mechanisms, indicating no generative model; however it highlights extensive pretraining (5M cells, 35B tokens), satisfying foundation‑model evidence.",
