./analysis/cross_agent_screening_agreement/unstable_reasoning_cases.csv:21:1272,Towards Applying Large Language Models to Complement Single-Cell Foundation Models,include_decision_unstable,EXCLUDE|EXCLUDE|EXCLUDE|UNCERTAIN,EXCLUDE,application_wrapper,,wrapper_boundary,none,none,none,"scMPT fuses scGPT and LLM representations without generating text or conditioning on natural-language input; it applies existing LLMs as complementary, fitting application_wrapper exclusion.",EXCLUDE,application_wrapper,,,,,,"The paper introduces scMPT, a fusion model that uses external LLM representations as side information to complement scGPT for single-cell analysis, fitting the application_wrapper exclusion. | The abstract describes scMPT as a fusion of scGPT and LLM representations for single-cell analysis, with no explicit generative mechanism; it is an application wrapper rather than a primary generative model.",EXCLUDE,EC3_not_generative,,,,,,"The paper introduces scMPT, a new model that fuses a single‑cell foundation model with LLM‑derived representations, establishing a substantive text‑bio multimodal bridge. | The abstract introduces scMPT, a model that fuses scGPT and LLM representations, but it does not mention any decoder, autoregressive, or other generative mechanism. It references foundation models (scGPT, LLMs) but does not provide evidence that scMPT itself is a broadly pretrained foundation model.",UNCERTAIN,,text_component_unclear,thin_abstract_boundary,none,"leverages synergies between scGPT, and single-cell representations from LLMs that capture these insights",none,"The abstract presents scMPT, a new model that fuses scGPT with LLM‑derived representations, indicating a bridge between text‑trained models and single‑cell data, but it does not explicitly describe natural‑language text input or generation, leaving the text component status uncertain.",thin_or_truncated_abstract;wrapper_boundary;text_component_boundary;generative_boundary
./analysis/cross_agent_screening_agreement/unstable_reasoning_cases.csv:30:3377,Cell2Sentence: teaching large language models the language of biology,stable_include,UNCERTAIN|EXCLUDE|INCLUDE|INCLUDE,UNCERTAIN,,text_component_unclear,thin_abstract_boundary,direct data-driven text generation,bridges the gap between natural language processing and biology,can generate biologically valid cells,"Paper presents Cell2Sentence fine-tuning GPT-2 on cell sentences. Text component and text-bio bridge are unclear because 'cell sentences' are biological token sequences, not natural-language text; text generation mention is ambiguous. Generative model is clear from cell generation and GPT-2 fine-tuning.",EXCLUDE,EC2_no_text_component,,text_component_boundary,direct data-driven text generation,transforming gene expression data into 'cell sentences',"cell generation, direct data-driven text generation","The abstract presents Cell2Sentence as a method to adapt LLMs to single-cell transcriptomics using cell sentences (biological tokens), not natural-language text. While the model is generative and uses GPT-2, the text component is not clearly natural language, so text_component_present=no and text_bio_bridge_present=no, leading to exclusion EC2_no_text_component. The paper is a primary model paper, not a wrapper, because it introduces a fine-tuning method.",INCLUDE,,,,,,,"The paper introduces Cell2Sentence, a novel method that converts single‑cell transcriptomics into natural‑language sentences and fine‑tunes GPT‑2 to generate biologically valid cells, demonstrating a clear text‑bio multimodal model. | The abstract introduces Cell2Sentence, fine‑tuning GPT‑2 to generate cells and text, showing a generative decoder architecture built on a pre‑trained large language model.",INCLUDE,,,,,,,"The abstract introduces Cell2Sentence, a new method that converts single‑cell transcriptomics into textual sentences and fine‑tunes GPT‑2, demonstrating generation of cells from text inputs and prediction of cell types from sentences; this constitutes a primary multimodal generative model linking natural language and biology. | The abstract reports fine‑tuning GPT‑2 (a decoder LLM) to generate cells and text, confirming a generative architecture; it also leverages a pre‑trained large language model, indicating foundation‑model properties.",thin_or_truncated_abstract;wrapper_boundary;text_component_boundary;generative_boundary;biological_token_only
./analysis/cross_agent_screening_agreement/research_memo_cross_agent_agreement.md:88:DeepSeek treats "cell sentences" as biological token sequences, not necessarily natural-language text. GPT-OSS interprets conversion into sentences and GPT-2 fine-tuning as a text-bio bridge.
