./data/docling_uncertain_biorxiv_chrome_no_vlm_2026-07-08/documents/rec_002228_2025_08_23_671699v2_full.docling.json:27617:      "orig": "are transformed into a one-hot encoded matrix, that essentially stores the information of whether each gene was present in the corresponding cell sentence (this transformation discards the rank-based order of the genes, thus resulting in some underestimation of the variation). This one-hot encoded matrix is then used for PCA analogously to the reference gene expression matrix reduced to 2000 highly variable genes. We additionally compare the size of the gene set included in the cell sentences of varying length. The results in Additional file 1, Fig. S1 show that a length of 50 genes includes sufficient variance in a specialist model setting, while obtaining computational efficiency.",
./data/docling_uncertain_biorxiv_chrome_no_vlm_2026-07-08/documents/rec_002228_2025_08_23_671699v2_full.docling.json:27618:      "text": "are transformed into a one-hot encoded matrix, that essentially stores the information of whether each gene was present in the corresponding cell sentence (this transformation discards the rank-based order of the genes, thus resulting in some underestimation of the variation). This one-hot encoded matrix is then used for PCA analogously to the reference gene expression matrix reduced to 2000 highly variable genes. We additionally compare the size of the gene set included in the cell sentences of varying length. The results in Additional file 1, Fig. S1 show that a length of 50 genes includes sufficient variance in a specialist model setting, while obtaining computational efficiency."
