./data/screening_codex_full_2026-07-06/role_logs/scope_reviewer/batch_0457.response.txt:1:{"results":[{"record_id":"rec_003649","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"none","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"Introduces HitAnno as a new hierarchical language model for atlas-level scATAC-seq annotation. The model builds “cell sentences” from peaks and uses attention over accessibility profiles.","evidence_snippet":"“hierarchical language model capable of accurate and scalable cell type annotation in atlas-level scATAC-seq data” and “construct ‘cell sentences’”"},{"record_id":"rec_003650","paper_type":"application_wrapper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"application_wrapper","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"Described as an AI-powered web platform with an LLM assistant for integrative transcriptomics analysis, not a new candidate model paper. The model use is framed as platform support.","evidence_snippet":"“OMICX: An AI-powered web platform” and “powered by a large language model (LLM) assistant”"},{"record_id":"rec_003651","paper_type":"benchmark_resource","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"benchmark_resource","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This is a curated atlas/resource of cell-marker annotations with a web platform, rather than a primary generative model. The LLM is used for literature curation and annotation support.","evidence_snippet":"“cell marker atlas” and “developed using an LLM-assisted literature-curation framework”"},{"record_id":"rec_003652","paper_type":"application_wrapper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"application_wrapper","uncertainty_reason":"mixed_signals","decision_rationale":"The title and fragment read as a multi-agent framework for multi-omics analysis, not a candidate model. The abstract snippet is incomplete and mixes framework language with a foundation-model reference.","evidence_snippet":"“A CONVERSATIONAL MULTI-AGENT AI FRAMEWORK” and fragment “refined by a lightweight language model”"},{"record_id":"rec_003653","paper_type":"application_wrapper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"application_wrapper","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This is a cell-annotation program that uses local generative AI and retrieval-augmented generation as a tool in the pipeline. It is presented as a streamlined application, not a new text-bio foundation model.","evidence_snippet":"“streamlined, scalable program” using “modern gen-AI models” and “retrieval augmented generation methods”"},{"record_id":"rec_003654","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC2_no_text_component","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The record describes a foundation model for bulk and single-cell RNA-seq, but no substantive text/language component is evident. The biological modality is clear, but the text criterion is not met.","evidence_snippet":"“first foundation model that can simultaneously learn from bulk RNA-seq and single-cell RNA-”"},{"record_id":"rec_003655","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC2_no_text_component","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This is a single-cell gene-expression completion model, with no clear text/language component in the title or abstract. The mention of scGPT is contextual and not the candidate model itself.","evidence_snippet":"“Sparse-Aware Diffusion Model for Single-Cell Gene Expression Completion”"},{"record_id":"rec_003656","paper_type":"review_editorial","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The abstract explicitly says this paper systematically reviews research progress and compares categories of medical foundation models. It is a review, not a primary model paper.","evidence_snippet":"“This paper systematically reviews the research progress” and “providing a systematic comparison”"}]}
