./data/screening_codex_full_2026-07-06/role_logs/scope_reviewer/batch_0320.stderr.log:1199:./data/screening_codex_full_2026-07-06/role_logs/scope_reviewer/batch_0319.stderr.log:108:{"results":[{"record_id":"rec_002545","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC2_no_text_component","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"Primary research on scFMs and their learned representations. The abstract describes sparse autoencoders on single-cell foundation model hidden states, but not a substantive language-model text component.","evidence_snippet":"\"training sparse autoencoders (SAEs) on the hidden representations of three widely used scFMs\""},{"record_id":"rec_002546","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"no","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC1_no_bio_modality","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This is a graph transformer prompt-tuning paper focused on graph topologies and molecular graph tasks. No biological data modality or text-bio bridge is described in the abstract.","evidence_snippet":"\"Graph Transformers\" and \"molecular graph classification and regression\""},{"record_id":"rec_002547","paper_type":"benchmark_resource","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"benchmark_resource","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The paper introduces scISP as an evaluation framework to benchmark existing foundation models for in-silico perturbation. This is a benchmarking/resource-style study rather than a new candidate model.","evidence_snippet":"\"We introduce a novel evaluation framework, the single cell in-silico perturbation framework (scISP), to benchmark ISP models\""},{"record_id":"rec_002548","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"none","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The abstract presents EpiAgent as a new foundation model for single-cell epigenomic data. It explicitly uses tokenized \"cell sentences\" and bidirectional attention, supporting a substantive bio-text bridge.","evidence_snippet":"\"we introduce EpiAgent, the first foundation model for single-cell epigenomic data\" and \"encodes chromatin accessibility patterns of cells as concise 'cell sentences'\""},{"record_id":"rec_002549","paper_type":"benchmark_resource","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"benchmark_resource","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This is a systematic benchmarking method, scFME, for evaluating fine-tuned foundation models on in-silico perturbation. The abstract emphasizes comparison and assessment rather than a new candidate model.","evidence_snippet":"\"we propose Single-Cell Foundation Model Evaluation (scFME)—a systematic method designed to benchmark fine-tuned foundation models\""},{"record_id":"rec_002550","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"unclear","text_bio_bridge_present":"unclear","primary_exclusion_code":"none","uncertainty_reason":"text_bio_bridge_unclear","decision_rationale":"The title indicates a single-cell epigenomic foundation model, but no abstract is provided to verify the model design or the strength of any text-bio bridge. Screening should stay permissive here.","evidence_snippet":"\"Deciphering single-cell epigenomic language with a foundation model\""},{"record_id":"rec_002551","paper_type":"benchmark_resource","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"benchmark_resource","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The abstract describes an evaluation and ablation study of existing single-cell RNA foundation models against baselines. It does not present a new generative text-bio model.","evidence_snippet":"\"we explore two foundation models recently developed for single-cell RNA sequencing data\" and \"compare[d] to a simple baseline\""},{"record_id":"rec_002552","paper_type":"benchmark_resource","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"benchmark_resource","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This paper systematically evaluates rare-cell detection tools and analytical strategies on scRNA-seq datasets. It is a benchmarking study, not a candidate model paper.","evidence_snippet":"\"We performed a comprehensive benchmarking analysis of five widely used rare cell detection tools\""}]}
