he recent five years\""},{"record_id":"rec_002503","paper_type":"application_wrapper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"application_wrapper","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"SpaLLM integrates pre-computed LLM embeddings of gene descriptions into spatial transcriptomics analysis. The abstract describes a modular feature-integration framework layered onto existing pipelines, not a primary text-bio foundation model.","evidence_snippet":"\"integrates large language model (LLM) embeddings of gene descriptions with conventional spatial transcriptomics analysis\"; \"can be seamlessly integrated with existing spatial analysis pipelines\""},{"record_id":"rec_002504","paper_type":"application_wrapper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"application_wrapper","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"GenePert uses GenePT embeddings derived from ChatGPT text descriptions of genes as inputs to regularized regression for perturbation prediction. That is downstream use of external text embeddings rather than a substantive new text-bio model.","evidence_snippet":"\"leverages GenePT embeddings, which are derived using ChatGPT from text descriptions of individual genes\"; \"predict gene expression changes ... via regularized regression models\""}]}
